# Root Cause

The vulnerability originated from inconsistent request processing between infrastructure components.

Specifically:

- The reverse proxy enforced access restrictions using the request URI.
- The application trusted the `X-Original-URL` header to determine the resource.
- Authorization was not revalidated after the URL rewrite.

This inconsistency enabled attackers to bypass the protection entirely.

---

# Impact

An attacker could:

- Bypass administrative access restrictions.
- Execute privileged functionality.
- Delete users.
- Modify sensitive data.
- Access administrative endpoints.
- Potentially achieve complete application compromise.

