# Security Recommendations

## Do Not Trust Client-Supplied Routing Headers

Headers such as:

- `X-Original-URL`
- `X-Rewrite-URL`
- `X-Forwarded-Prefix`

must never be trusted when received directly from external clients.

These headers should only be generated internally by trusted infrastructure.

---

## Perform Authorization After URL Rewriting

Authorization decisions must be performed against the final resource actually processed by the application.

---

## Strip Internal Headers at the Proxy

Reverse proxies should remove externally supplied internal routing headers.

Example (Nginx):

```nginx
proxy_set_header X-Original-URL "";
proxy_set_header X-Rewrite-URL "";
```

---

## Use a Single Source of Truth

All components in the request path should evaluate the same effective URL before authorizing access.

---

## Log Suspicious Routing Headers

Generate security alerts when external clients send unexpected headers such as:

```text
X-Original-URL
X-Rewrite-URL
X-Forwarded-Prefix
```

